{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>A remembrance for the children of Israel, so that no stranger draw near.</b> From this we learn that the matter was told to Moses, that he should tell Aaron, so that whoever sees it would ask. As it is written: ״מזבח אדמה תעשה לי״ — they would fill its hollow with earth. If so, what is the point of its having a copper plate? And the one who is asked answers: this plate was made from the firepans of Korah and his assembly, who were challenging the priesthood, and all the people will hear and fear to challenge again." "<b>By Moses' hand, lo.</b> To Korah. And its meaning is: concerning Korah — as an example, like ״כי לא אעזבך עד אשר אם עשיתי את אשר דברתי לך,״ which means: what I spoke concerning you. Another interpretation: lo — to Aaron."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:18:21.837534713Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}